[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read report by report, it
held three problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October with two changes: the parser fix
(`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`) and retiring the booking-v3 form. Neither touches the
third problem.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but bookings still move by one day. That problem is open in its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 held

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser read dates month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day
first, so "7 April" came out as "4 July". This is the bug #4471 named. **Fixed** on 5 October.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form told people to type the month first.** Its date field printed
`MM/DD/YYYY`, but the form read what people typed the tenant's way, day first. People did what the
hint said and the date flipped. Same symptom as `parser`, different code: the parser fix did not
touch it. **Won't fix**: the booking-v3 form is retired, so the hint is gone with it.

**`move`: the booking lands one day off.** Day and month are not swapped. The same meeting shows
on different days in Lisbon and Toronto, and one tenant sees it only in June. That points at time
zones, not at date order, so neither change on 5 October covers it. The desk read these as a
one-day move and counts them under `parser` by tenant, so they had no ticket. **Open.**

## How we told them apart

- By the tenant (its locale and booking form, `locales.ts`) and the channel, not by intake's tag.
  Intake tags by the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the tenant often: it tags en-US
  browsers as `hint`, which catches about half of the real `hint` reports and mislabels a set of
  `parser` reports.
- By what the dates in the report do: a swap (day ↔ month) or a one-day move.
- Counted the way the desk's own view counts them, from the export of 4 October. Duplicate rows
  count once, by report id.

## Lessons

- Matching on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) merges by symptom.
  Different bugs with the same symptom end up in one ticket, and closing it closes all of them.
- Before a big ticket is marked known or closed, check its reports against the cause, not the
  subject.

